🔹 1. Pivot Table (for Reporting/Aggregation)
➡️ Used for transforming rows into columns, as explained earlier (used in data analysis/reporting).

✅ What is a Pivot Table (in SQL)?
A pivot table is a way to transform rows into columns in SQL, summarizing data for reporting and analytics. It’s commonly used to aggregate data and display it in a more readable matrix or table format.

📊 Example:
Suppose you have a sales table:

| Region | Month | Revenue |
| ------ | ----- | ------- |
| East   | Jan   | 1000    |
| West   | Jan   | 1500    |
| East   | Feb   | 1200    |
| West   | Feb   | 1300    |


👉 Pivoted Output:
| Region | Jan  | Feb  |
| ------ | ---- | ---- |
| East   | 1000 | 1200 |
| West   | 1500 | 1300 |




✅ Summary:
| Term                            | Meaning                                              |
| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| **Pivot table (SQL/reporting)** | Transforms rows into columns for analytics           |
| **Pivot table (DB design)**     | Middle/junction table for many-to-many relationships |
